\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22\lang9 # Project Handover: Solana Automated Trading Bot \f1\emdash  Existing Codebase\par
\par
Act as a senior Node.js, Solana blockchain, and automated trading engineer. I already have an existing trading bot backend. Your job is to understand the current codebase, identify what is complete and incomplete, and help me finish it safely for a live client demonstration.\par
\par
**Important:** Do not rebuild the project from scratch. Inspect the existing code first, preserve working functionality, and make changes incrementally.\par
\par
## 1. Project Goal\par
\par
I want an automated Solana token trading bot that can:\par
\par
- Monitor market data and generate BUY/SELL signals using a strategy.\par
- Apply risk management before executing trades.\par
- Automatically buy tokens when buy conditions are satisfied.\par
- Automatically sell tokens when sell conditions are satisfied.\par
- Execute real on-chain transactions through the platform/API selected by the client.\par
- Verify actual transaction status, token amounts received, SOL spent/received, fees, and profit/loss.\par
- Update trade history, positions, and portfolio records correctly.\par
- Support a live demonstration to a client.\par
\par
The target trading platform needs to be confirmed with the project owner before finalizing platform-specific integration. Jupiter Swap API V2 has been investigated previously, but confirm whether Jupiter is the final target before assuming it.\par
\par
There is no frontend dashboard requirement at present. The priority is a working backend/API demonstration.\par
\par
