## 4. Existing REAL trading implementation and limitations\par
\par
### REAL BUY\par
\par
`services/realTradeExecutionService.js` exists.\par
\par
The inspected code includes these checks:\par
\par
- `TRADING_NETWORK` must equal `"mainnet"`.\par
- `getSolanaNetwork()` must return `"mainnet-beta"`.\par
- `JUPITER_API_KEY` must be configured.\par
\par
The service appears to create a PENDING trade, call `executeJupiterSwap`, and process the result.\par
\par
However, successful Mainnet execution has NOT been verified. Do not label REAL BUY as production-ready until a successful transaction and actual wallet changes are confirmed.\par
\par
### REAL SELL\par
\par
`services/sellExecutionService.js` currently rejects non-PAPER mode with:\par
\par
`REAL trade execution is not implemented yet`\par
\par
The inspected REAL execution service also rejects sides other than BUY.\par
\par
Therefore, REAL SELL is incomplete and needs implementation and testing.\par
\par
### Important BUY quantity inconsistency\par
\par
In `services/buyExecutionService.js`, the REAL branch calls `executeRealTrade` with:\par
\par
- `side: "BUY"`\par
- `solAmount: quantity`\par
\par
The PAPER branch uses `quantity` as token quantity, while the REAL branch treats it as SOL spend.\par
\par
Inspect all callers, request validation, strategy calculations, models, and API routes before changing this. Establish explicit units for SOL spend, token quantity, token decimals, and USD price. Avoid introducing regressions.\par
\par
